1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Your headlights look brighter than usual at night.
That's not always a good sign.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Dash lights flicker or seem too bright.
The battery case looks a little swollen.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
One clue: the alternator can overcharge the battery —
pushing more voltage than it should.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
That extra voltage can cook a battery from the inside —
long before it ever looks dead.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Don't guess at the voltage.
A quick test can show what the charging system is actually doing.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before it costs you a battery.
Stop by and we'll take a look. Nick's Tire & Auto.
